#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:1
msgid "ADR-0009: Double precision by default and JAX as the first GPU backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P4.11 (benchmarks, revisiting REQ-HPC-5 and ADR-0004)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:9
msgid ""
"The GPU benchmarks of P4.11 raised two questions: should LUMOS compute in"
" single precision by default to be faster, and should JAX stay the "
"preferred GPU backend (ADR-0004) although it was measured 2 to 3 times "
"slower than CuPy on the same GPU?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:13
msgid ""
"Measurements on a GeForce GTX 1060 (consumer GPU, double precision at "
"1/32 of the single-precision rate) and an 8-core CPU, reported in "
"`docs/learn/performance.md`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:16
msgid ""
"**Single precision speed**: padded FFTs (angular spectrum, Fresnel "
"transfer function) are limited by memory bandwidth: single precision "
"makes them about 2 times faster on the CPU and 3 times faster on the GPU."
" Matrix Fourier transforms are limited by arithmetic: 13 to 23 times "
"faster on this GPU, 1.5 to 2 times on the CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:20
msgid ""
"**Single precision accuracy**: fields agree with double precision within "
"about 1e-6 of their peak once every kernel is computed in double "
"precision and rounded once (fixed for the MFT chirps in this step: a "
"phase such as `k z` reaches 1e4 to 1e7 rad, which float32 resolves only "
"to 1e-3 to 1 rad). Running the test suite in single precision fails 125 "
"of its 1000 tests, whose tolerances (1e-10 to 1e-12 for energy "
"conservation, unitarity, reciprocity, nulls) assume double precision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:25
msgid ""
"**JAX**: run operation by operation (\"eager\"), each JAX operation is "
"dispatched separately and a LUMOS propagation is 1.4 (N = 1024) to 7 (N ="
" 256) times slower than with CuPy; compiled with `jax.jit`, the same "
"propagation is as fast as CuPy or faster (17.8 ms against 25.9 ms for a "
"1024 × 1024 angular spectrum). The gap was the eager dispatch, not JAX "
"itself. The first CuPy times were also too short, because the benchmark "
"did not wait for CuPy's asynchronous kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:30
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:32
msgid ""
"**Double precision stays the default** (`lumos.config.precision = "
"\"double\"`); single precision is an opt-in for speed. Whatever the "
"precision, kernels (transfer functions, chirps, MFT matrices) are "
"computed in double precision and rounded once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:35
msgid ""
"**JAX stays the first GPU backend** of `\"auto\"` (ADR-0004 unchanged): "
"compiled, it matches CuPy and it is differentiable. CuPy remains the GPU "
"backend on native Windows, where JAX has no GPU build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:37
msgid ""
"Pipelines run on JAX should be compiled: users compile their own "
"functions with `lumos.jit`, and the execution of a context should compile"
" its pure transfer chain on JAX when this becomes possible (ADR-0006)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:40
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:42
msgid ""
"LUMOS targets high-contrast instruments (nulling interferometry, "
"coronagraphy) whose signals are 1e-5 to 1e-10 of the starlight: the "
"round-off of single precision (about 1e-6 of the peak field, 1e-12 in "
"intensity after one propagation) is close to these levels after a chain "
"of elements, and accumulates in long simulations (turbulence time series,"
" optimisation loops, finite-difference gradients)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:46
msgid ""
"The speed-up of single precision is modest where most of the time is "
"spent (padded FFTs: 2 to 3 times) and large only for matrix Fourier "
"transforms on consumer GPUs; professional GPUs (A100, H100) compute in "
"double precision at half or full single-precision rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:49
msgid ""
"A single-precision default would not simplify the tests: their tolerances"
" would have to be loosened by four to six orders of magnitude, hiding "
"real errors such as the lost `k z` phase found here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:51
msgid ""
"REQ-HPC-5 asks for a configurable precision, and the `.lumos` format "
"records `complex128` as the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:53
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:55
msgid ""
"**Single precision by default**: faster on consumer GPUs, but silently "
"inaccurate for the main use cases, and incompatible with the current test"
" tolerances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:57
msgid ""
"**Precision chosen by backend** (single on GPUs, double on CPUs): results"
" would depend on the hardware, contradicting REQ-HPC-1 (identical results"
" on every backend within floating-point tolerances)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:59
msgid ""
"**CuPy as the first GPU backend**: faster without compilation, but not "
"differentiable, and it would give different execution paths for "
"optimisation (JAX) and simulation (CuPy)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:62
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:64
msgid ""
"Users who want speed on consumer GPUs set `lumos.config.precision = "
"\"single\"` and accept a relative error of about 1e-6; the documentation "
"says when this is safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:66
msgid ""
"Eager LUMOS code is slower on JAX than on CuPy until context execution "
"compiles its pipelines; the performance page shows how to compile with "
"`lumos.jit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0009-precision-and-gpu-backend.md:68
msgid ""
"New kernels must be computed in double precision on the host or with "
"explicit float64 coordinates, never from coordinates in the working "
"precision; `tests/physics/test_propagation_precision.py` checks this for "
"the propagation methods."
msgstr ""
